Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-05
Subject: Make TPaiProp.Create an explicit override for FPC 3.2.0
License: expat

TPaiProp.Create has the same signature as the inherited virtual
TAoptBase.Create constructor.  tp2cc lowers Pascal objects to C++ classes,
where a same-signature derived method overrides the inherited virtual slot.

The 3.2.0 compiler source has no live TPaiProp descendant or class-reference
construction path that depends on hiding TAoptBase.Create.  Mark the
constructor as override so the Pascal declaration matches the dispatch
semantics that the generated C++ can represent.

--- a/compiler/aoptobj.pas
+++ b/compiler/aoptobj.pas
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ Unit AoptObj;
         { can this instruction be removed? }
         CanBeRemoved: Boolean;
 
-        Constructor create; reintroduce;
+        Constructor create; override;
 
         { checks the whole sequence of which (so regs[which].StartMod and and  }
         { the next NrOfMods Tai objects) to see whether Reg is used somewhere, }
